WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.158
A running total is another common window-function
pattern Instead of collapsing

00:00:06.184 --> 00:00:09.197
sales by date we can keep each date or row in
sequence

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:14.215
while showing the cumulative revenue up to that
point The ORDER BY

00:00:14.241 --> 00:00:20.297
inside the window defines the progression of the
calculation Run the example

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:25.467
and watch the running total increase as the dates
move forward This

00:00:25.494 --> 00:00:31.073
pattern appears in financial balances cumulative
enrollment inventory movement project progress

00:00:31.296 --> 00:00:36.968
and many other time-ordered analyses When you build
a running total make

00:00:36.995 --> 00:00:41.839
sure the ordering is deterministic If multiple rows
can share the same

00:00:41.853 --> 00:00:45.458
date think about whether you need an additional
ordering column to define

00:00:45.484 --> 00:00:46.603
a stable sequence
